1
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:18,800
This is two-minute ideas from ideas in English, and this idea is about missing out.

2
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,800
A common fear these days is FOMO.

3
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:30,269
FOMO is quite a new word in English, and it stands for fear of missing out.

4
00:00:30,269 --> 00:00:41,060
It's the fear that you might not get something you want, that you won't be able to do all the things you want to do in life,

5
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:47,369
or that good things are happening somewhere else, and you're missing out.

6
00:00:47,369 --> 00:00:59,740
And FOMO seems to have increased with social media, as people share their best moments, and we can see more of what everyone else is doing,

7
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:03,320
or at least what they're showing us they're doing.

8
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:16,459
But there's an even newer word that's the opposite of FOMO, and that's JOMO, which stands for the joy of missing out.

9
00:01:16,459 --> 00:01:22,219
JOMO is feeling happy that you're not doing all the exciting things,

10
00:01:22,219 --> 00:01:29,290
and it's letting go of the stressful idea that you could, or should, be doing more.

11
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:39,989
You can't do everything, and, as journalist Oliver Bergman explains,

12
00:01:39,989 --> 00:01:46,120
JOMO is a good feeling when you realize that you wouldn't actually want to.

13
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:51,019
You have to make choices in life about what to do,

14
00:01:51,019 --> 00:01:59,549
and Bergman says that it's the fact that you can't do everything that makes your choices meaningful.

15
00:01:59,549 --> 00:02:08,370
You can choose to do something, or something else, or not do it.

16
00:02:08,370 --> 00:02:11,370
Take care, and good luck with the learning.
